course: dictionary
lesson: 9900
title: Who are the Taliban?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The Taliban is a group of people, not a country, so the word is a proper noun and needs a capital letter. You will often see it in news reports about Afghanistan. Look at the words around it to work out what it means.
explain: The Taliban is a militant political and religious group in Afghanistan. Militant means it is willing to use force and fighting to get what it wants. It ruled most of Afghanistan from 1996 to 2001 and took power again in 2021.
explain: «As widely reported, Malala Yousafzai spoke up for girls' education in Pakistan, was attacked by the Taliban in 2012, survived, and won the Nobel Peace Prize at 17.» The sentence shows the Taliban as a group that opposed girls going to school. Malala's story is about a brave girl who spoke up, and she survived.
explain: Phrases help too. «The Taliban government» means the government run by this group, and «under the Taliban» means living while this group is in charge. Most Afghans are not part of the Taliban, so do not think the word describes everyone from Afghanistan.
fact: The Taliban is a proper noun, so it starts with a capital letter.
fact: The Taliban is a militant political and religious group in Afghanistan.
fact: The Taliban ruled most of Afghanistan from 1996 to 2001 and took power again in 2021.
fact: Many people, including the United Nations, criticise the Taliban for very harsh rules, especially stopping girls and women from going to secondary school, university and many jobs.
fact: Most Afghans and most Muslims are not part of the Taliban.
exercise: «As widely reported, Malala Yousafzai spoke up for girls' education in Pakistan, was attacked by the Taliban in 2012.» What is the Taliban in this sentence? | A famous school for girls | A prize for brave people | A country in Asia | *A militant political and religious group in Afghanistan
exercise: What does «the Taliban government» mean? | A government that helps all girls go to school | A new name for a school | A government in Pakistan | *The government run by the Taliban group
exercise: Why is the Taliban widely criticised? | They are a football team | *Their very harsh rules, especially stopping girls and women from school and many jobs | They won a Nobel Peace Prize | They built many new schools for girls
test: Why was Malala attacked by the Taliban? | Because she won a prize | Because she was playing football in the street | *Because she spoke up for girls' education | Because she was a famous teacher
test: Is it true that most Afghans are part of the Taliban? | Yes, only the children are part of it | Yes, every Afghan is part of it | *No, most Afghans are not part of it | Yes, but only since 2021
exam: Between which years did the Taliban rule most of Afghanistan for a time? | 2012 to 2014 | *1996 to 2001 | 1800 to 1850 | 1914 to 1918
